1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,752
The Blackmar-Diemer offers a pawn to open lines fast.

2
00:00:04,912 --> 00:00:09,365
Black accepts, but the queen side is still asleep.

3
00:00:09,525 --> 00:00:13,977
The knight attacks the center and keeps the initiative.

4
00:00:14,137 --> 00:00:18,590
White pushes f three and turns the position tactical.

5
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:23,203
Black captures, but the recapturing knight gains a tempo.

6
00:00:23,363 --> 00:00:27,815
The e pawn builds a solid shell around the king.

7
00:00:27,975 --> 00:00:32,428
White develops the bishop to pin the knight.

8
00:00:32,587 --> 00:00:37,040
Black blocks the diagonal with a calm developing move.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,652
The second bishop joins and points at the king side.

10
00:00:41,812 --> 00:00:46,265
Both kings castle, but White has the easier plan.

11
00:00:46,425 --> 00:00:50,877
The lesson: open lines are worth more when pieces are ready.

12
00:00:51,037 --> 00:00:55,650
Would you play the pawn sacrifice?

